  "summary": "Preprints on emulators, differentiable bispectra, cluster pipelines and GW sirens target LSST Year 1 and next-generation analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is preparing theory and inference infrastructure for LSST-era and next-generation surveys. Hi-COLA trains an emulator for the nonlinear matter power spectrum in Cubic Galileon gravity, validated for LSST Year 1 weak lensing and clustering. bihalofit-JAX provides a differentiable nonlinear bispectrum code with projected statistics. The LSST DESC cluster pipeline is validated on cosmoDC2 mocks, constraining Omega_c and sigma_8. A cubic-order EFT forward model for the Lyman-alpha forest is validated on CAMELS and Sherwood simulations, with BAO shift predictions. Gravitational-wave items are more peripheral: Padé-approximant cosmography forecasts for LISA, Einstein Telescope and DECIGO standard sirens, and QCD equation-of-state effects on expansion and the stochastic GW spectrum.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
